Not a real file to add as-is — this is a diff note for xpcom/ds/StaticAtoms.py
(a large stock Mozilla file; only a single atom entry is added).

REAL BUG, found via a real boot (2026-07-06): JSWindowActor `matches:
["pyxis://*/*"]` (toolkit/modules/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs's PyxisBridge
entry) silently NEVER matched any pyxis:// document, even though the
document itself loaded correctly (confirmed via an fprintf canary in
PyxisProtocolHandler::NewChannel showing pyxis://bloom/index.html + its
JS/CSS/favicon all being fetched normally, and separately confirming via
console.error canaries in both PyxisBridgeChild's and PyxisBridgeParent's
actorCreated() that neither ever fired). Root cause, traced into
toolkit/components/extensions/MatchPattern.cpp's MatchPatternCore
constructor: it consults a hardcoded `HostLocatorSchemes()` atom set to
decide whether a scheme uses "scheme://host/path" syntax (requiring host
parsing) vs "scheme:path" syntax (about:, data:, etc. — no host, path
matched literally against everything after the colon). "pyxis" was not in
that atom set, so the constructor treated the "//*/*" tail of our pattern as
a literal PATH to match — which can never match a real
pyxis://<app-id>/<path> URI's actual path (which never begins with "//").
No error was thrown; the pattern just quietly matched nothing, ever.

Fix requires a new nsGkAtoms atom (StaticAtoms.py has no "pyxis" atom yet)
plus referencing it in HostLocatorSchemes() — see the companion diff note at
gecko/patches/pyxis/toolkit/components/extensions/MatchPattern.cpp.PYXIS_DIFF.

Add, near the existing WebExtensions atom (real precedent: `moz-extension`
is the only other non-built-in scheme already in this file, and is also the
one HostLocatorSchemes() entry closest to Pyxis's needs):

    Atom("pyxis", "pyxis"),

placed directly after:

    Atom("moz_extension", "moz-extension"),

(inside the `# WebExtensions` section of the big Atom(...) list — exact line
number drifts across pulls, search for `moz_extension` to find it).
